5. SAFETY NOTICE AND LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

   THIS FIRMWARE SWITCHES MAINS ELECTRICITY SUPPLIED TO A DOMESTIC
   WATER HEATER (GEYSER), BY DRIVING A RELAY ON A LIVE CIRCUIT.
   Incorrect wiring, assembly, configuration or use can cause electric
   shock, fire, burns, scalding, water damage, property damage, serious
   injury or death.

   Specific hazards include, without limitation: contact with live
   conductors during assembly or servicing; relay or contactor failure
   leaving the element energised; loss or failure of the temperature
   sensor; failure of any software interlock, thermostat limit or
   run-time cutoff; and interaction with the water heater's own
   thermostat, pressure-relief valve and earth-leakage protection.

   The Software has not been certified, approved or tested against any
   electrical safety standard. It carries no safety integrity rating,
   and it must not be treated as a protective device. It is published
   for inspection and experimentation only, and it is not fit for
   installation in a dwelling relied upon by anyone.

   Electrical work must be carried out by a suitably qualified and,
   where required, licensed person, in accordance with the wiring rules
   and regulations applicable in Your jurisdiction. Isolate the supply
   before working on any circuit. You are solely responsible for
   compliance, and for any certificate of compliance your jurisdiction
   requires.

   TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL
   THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, LOSS OR OTHER
   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT
   OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR ITS USE. YOU ASSUME THE
   ENTIRE RISK OF BUILDING, FLASHING, WIRING AND OPERATING IT.

   Nothing in this licence excludes or limits liability that cannot
   lawfully be excluded or limited.


